circle-rp1dsi.patch (Sidecar): the Raspberry Pi Touch Display 2 (5" and 7") on the Pi 5 with Circle's addon/rp1dsi.
The DSI host takes the panel's mode flags (the v2 default is VIDEO|LPM, sync events, as Linux; the v1 display keeps its
own), dropped commands and each bring-up step are logged, the GT911 is probed on both addresses with its contact id
bounded, and the v2 panel size can be forced (g_nRPiTouchScreen2Panel). The Pi 4 and the v1 display are not changed.

